[
  {
    "version": "v0.9",
    "createSurface": {
      "surfaceId": "story_surface",
      "catalogId": "https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json"
    }
  },
  {
    "version": "v0.9",
    "updateComponents": {
      "surfaceId": "story_surface",
      "components": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "type": "Column",
          "properties": {
            "children": [
              "story_card"
            ],
            "padding": {
              "all": "medium"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "story_card",
          "type": "Card",
          "properties": {
            "children": [
              "story_title",
              "story_tabs"
            ],
            "padding": {
              "all": "large"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "story_title",
          "type": "Text",
          "properties": {
            "text": "The Clockmaker's Five Seconds",
            "style": "heading",
            "align": "center"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "story_tabs",
          "type": "Tabs",
          "properties": {
            "tabs": [
              {
                "label": "The Setting",
                "child": "tab_setting"
              },
              {
                "label": "The Discovery",
                "child": "tab_discovery"
              },
              {
                "label": "The Incident",
                "child": "tab_incident"
              },
              {
                "label": "The Miracle",
                "child": "tab_miracle"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "tab_setting",
          "type": "Column",
          "properties": {
            "children": [
              "setting_icon",
              "setting_text"
            ],
            "spacing": "medium",
            "padding": {
              "top": "large"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "setting_icon",
          "type": "Icon",
          "properties": {
            "icon": "clock",
            "size": "large",
            "align": "center"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "setting_text",
          "type": "Text",
          "properties": {
            "text": "Josef Kovář, a man whose hands moved with the precision of the gears he meticulously crafted, owned a small, unassuming clock shop nestled in the labyrinthine alleys of Prague in the year 1895. His shop, \"Časové Kouzlo\" (Time's Magic), was a sanctuary of ticking, chiming, and the gentle whir of unseen mechanisms. Josef, a bachelor in his late forties, lived for the intricate dance of springs and cogs."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "tab_discovery",
          "type": "Column",
          "properties": {
            "children": [
              "discovery_icon",
              "discovery_text_1",
              "discovery_text_2"
            ],
            "spacing": "medium",
            "padding": {
              "top": "large"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "discovery_icon",
          "type": "Icon",
          "properties": {
            "icon": "sparkle",
            "size": "large",
            "align": "center"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "discovery_text_1",
          "type": "Text",
          "properties": {
            "text": "One crisp autumn evening, while disassembling an antique pocket watch brought in by a reclusive count, Josef discovered a peculiar additional mechanism. It was a tiny, almost invisible lever, connected to a crystal that pulsed with a faint, otherworldly blue light when activated. Driven by an insatiable curiosity, Josef spent weeks studying it, sacrificing sleep and meals. Finally, with a trembling hand, he pressed the lever."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "discovery_text_2",
          "type": "Text",
          "properties": {
            "text": "The world around him froze. The pendulum of the grandfather clock in the corner hung mid-swing, a dust motes suspended in the air like tiny, frozen stars, and the distant clatter of a horse-drawn carriage from outside vanished into an absolute silence. Josef, however, could move freely. He checked his own pocket watch – exactly five seconds had passed when the world snapped back into motion. He had stumbled upon a device that could halt time itself, for precisely five seconds. He named it the \"Chronos Shard.\""
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "tab_incident",
          "type": "Column",
          "properties": {
            "children": [
              "incident_icon",
              "incident_text"
            ],
            "spacing": "medium",
            "padding": {
              "top": "large"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "incident_icon",
          "type": "Icon",
          "properties": {
            "icon": "alert-triangle",
            "size": "large",
            "align": "center"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "incident_text",
          "type": "Text",
          "properties": {
            "text": "A week later, the Chronos Shard found its purpose. Josef was perched precariously on a tall stool, reaching for a rare, gilded cuckoo clock on a high shelf. Below him, his young apprentice, Karel, was meticulously polishing a display case filled with delicate porcelain figurines. As Josef stretched, his elbow accidentally nudged a stack of finely crafted wooden gears he had left on the edge of his workbench. They teetered, threatening to cascade down onto Karel and the fragile porcelain below. A scream caught in Karel's throat as he looked up, eyes wide with horror."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "tab_miracle",
          "type": "Column",
          "properties": {
            "children": [
              "miracle_icon",
              "miracle_text_1",
              "miracle_text_2"
            ],
            "spacing": "medium",
            "padding": {
              "top": "large"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "miracle_icon",
          "type": "Icon",
          "properties": {
            "icon": "shield-check",
            "size": "large",
            "align": "center"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "miracle_text_1",
          "type": "Text",
          "properties": {
            "text": "Without a moment's hesitation, Josef's hand flew to his waistcoat pocket, retrieving the Chronos Shard. He pressed the lever. The world immediately plunged into silence and stillness. Karel was frozen, one hand reaching out in a futile attempt to catch the falling gears. Josef moved with practiced haste, stepping off the stool, gently intercepting the gears mid-air, and placing them safely back on the workbench. He then subtly nudged Karel's polishing cloth a fraction of an inch further, making it appear as though the apprentice had simply paused in his work."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "miracle_text_2",
          "type": "Text",
          "properties": {
            "text": "Five seconds later, the world resumed. The gears were safe, Karel blinked, looking confused, and Josef merely cleared his throat. \"Careful there, Karel,\" he said, feigning a slight wobble as he descended the stool, \"almost had a tumble.\" Karel, still a little pale, nodded, none the wiser, and continued polishing, oblivious to the near disaster, or the silent, five-second miracle that had just occurred. Josef merely smiled, a secret keeper of time's brief pause, in the heart of old Prague."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }
]
